  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-system1",
      "text": "**Connect to multiple decision providers and models through one interface: Jev via TypeSafe, Clef via Cloudflare, Drex via Nace, Decider 1 via meraGPT, self-hosted Laya, and compatible custom providers.** Agents and plugins can classify content, filter candidates, score against criteria, or locate objects in images, then use structured results in their own workflows. Requests can include text, images, audio, and video where the provider and model support them. The agent can call the built-in `system1_decide` tool, and plugins can use the same service through `ctx.system1.decide()`."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-system1",
      "text": "[](https://github.com/exoticknight/dsh-system1/actions/workflows/check.yml) [](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-system1) [](LICENSE) [](https://github.com/exoticknight/red)\n\n[](https://dsh.pub/en/plugins/?q=exoticknight%2Fdsh-system1) [](https://dsh-plugin.org/plugins/exoticknight/dsh-system1)\n[](https://unstone.github.io/dsh-xray/p/exoticknight__dsh-system1.html) [](https://dsh.market/) [](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com)\n\nEnglish | [简体中文](README.zh-CN.md)\n\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Providers and models",
      "text": "Choose a built-in provider or add one that implements the public provider contract. Model options and supported inputs vary by provider and model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Providers and models",
      "text": "| Provider | Model options | Deployment and notable support |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| TypeSafe (`typesafe`) | `jev-latest`, `jev-preview`, `jev-1.14.0`, `jev-1.13.0` | Hosted Jev; PNG/JPEG; `box` requires `jev-1.14.0` or `jev-preview`; optional 262k context. |\n| Cloudflare (`cloudflare`) | `clef`, `clef-flash`, `clef-omni` | Workers AI or a compatible local Clef service; PNG/JPEG/WebP; `clef-omni` also accepts audio and video. |\n| Nace.AI (`nace`) | `drex-v2.0`, `drex-v1.5`, `drex-max`, `drex-max-v1.1`, `drex-max-finance` | Hosted Drex; all three Max models accept images, up to 512 questions and 255 choice/score options. Original Max selects from state up to 524k tokens, allows 262k per question and caps combined long questions at 1,048,576; v1.1 and Finance cap the whole request at 262k; Finance specializes in financial decisions. |\n| meraGPT (`meragpt`) | `decider-1` (`sd-1`, `state-decider-1`) | Hosted Decider 1; 4k-token whole-request context, up to 64 questions and 10 choice/score options. Uses prepaid API credit. |\n| Laya (`laya`) | `auto`, `english`, `multilingual`, `typed-decisions` | Self-hosted [Laya server](https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya); text only; API key optiona"
    },
    {
      "section": "Providers and models",
      "text": "See [provider setup](docs/providers.en.md) for credentials, endpoints, and full capability limits.\n\n[System One models](https://systemonemodels.org/guides/what-is-a-system-one-model/) are decision models that return typed answers with probabilities instead of generated text. The name borrows Kahneman's \"fast thinking\": they handle narrow judgments such as gating, routing, and scoring, while the main LLM writes and reasons."
    },
    {
      "section": "Providers and models",
      "text": "| Primitive | Result                                                               |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `noul`    | Yes/no: probability that the proposition is true (`probabilityTrue`) |\n| `choice`  | Candidate key and the full probability distribution                  |\n| `score`   | Expected zero-based level and the probability distribution           |\n| `box`     | Normalized image coordinates for a located object (model-dependent)  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Providers and models",
      "text": "Requests and responses are validated, and each question gets its own result. Calls support cancellation, per-attempt timeouts, and fallback models, and return execution metadata."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from npm",
      "text": "Install the package in a project that uses System One:\n\n```sh\nnpm install dsh-system1\n```\n\nTo activate the bundled service and providers in dsh, add the npm package to the profile you run. Replace `<profile>` with your profile name:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add dsh-system1\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from npm",
      "text": "The dsh plugin command requires a profile; installing into one profile does not activate the bundle in other profiles. To use the GitHub repository as the package source, replace `dsh-system1` in that command with `github:exoticknight/dsh-system1`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from npm",
